{"id":"169b041b15ffad6fe22db2254fd082bee15f55ed","axis":"silent","repo":"symfony/symfony","sha":"169b041b15ffad6fe22db2254fd082bee15f55ed","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"UPGRADE-8.2.md","lines":["@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@ HttpClient"," ","  * [BC BREAK] Widen the type of the `$buffer` argument of `HttpOptions::buffer()` from `bool` to `mixed`, so that the stream and closure forms the option accepts can be passed; a class extending `HttpOptions` and overriding that method must widen it too","  * [BC BREAK] An explicit `http_version` of `2.0` makes `CurlHttpClient` and `AmpHttpClient` require HTTP/2: they use prior knowledge on `http://` URLs instead of offering an upgrade, and offer only `h2` during the TLS handshake on `https://` URLs (with curl 8.10 or higher); servers that speak only HTTP/1.1 are not reachable that way anymore, unset the option for them","+ * [BC BREAK] Redirects from `https://` to `http://` URLs are not followed anymore. The 3xx response is returned instead, and its `redirect_url` info contains the target URL. Request that URL yourself if you want to follow the redirect","  * `KernelTestCase::ensureKernelShutdown()` now clears the responses cached in the `cache.http_client` pool when `framework.test` is enabled, so that each test starts with no cached response. A test that relied on a response cached by a previous test, or before a kernel shutdown in the same test, should request it itself"," "," HttpFoundation"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/Symfony/Component/HttpClient/CHANGELOG.md","lines":["@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@ CHANGELOG","  * Add support for the `on_trailers` request option to `GuzzleHttpHandler`","  * Allow passing the `query` and `body` options as lists of single-entry arrays to repeat a field","  * Make `http_version: 2.0` use HTTP/2 with prior knowledge on `http://` URLs in `CurlHttpClient` and `AmpHttpClient`","+ * Stop following redirects from `https://` to `http://` URLs"," "," 8.1"," ---"],"additions":1,"deletions":